<title>SOUTH AFRICA: EASTERN S.AFRICAN PROVINCE HIT BY POWER FAILURE.</title>
<headline>EASTERN S.AFRICAN PROVINCE HIT BY POWER FAILURE.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electricity supplier Eskom said on Tuesday that a significant part of the eastern province of Mpumalanga had been hit by a power failure early on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;A technical fault occurred in a transformer at Camden substation feeding Ermelo, Wesselton, Estansia township and several mines in the area,&quot; Eskom said in a statement.</p>
<p>Technicians are working to connect up a spare transformer to restore power during the course of the day.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
